  "notes": "Modified cash basis city; basis recorded as cash. Governmental roll-forward uses fund balances from the governmental funds statement (p5): 1,580,729 + 1,724,296 - 1,272,919 - 149,496 (transfers to other funds, net) = 1,882,610; beginning_cash/ending_cash therefore hold fund balances (which include notes receivable and due-from-other-funds net of cash overdraft). Business-type uses the Proprietary Fund Statement of Revenues, Expenses and Changes in Net Position (p7): 3,146,518 + 526,801 - 391,398 + 149,496 = 3,431,417. That proprietary net position (3,431,417) differs from the government-wide cash-basis business-type net position (2,312,681, p1/p3) because the proprietary statements are on a different basis; both printed as is. Business-type receipts/disbursements totals computed (no single total printed). Balance sheet = government-wide Statement of Net Position (p1), Total column; bonds payable appear only on proprietary statement p6 (not used). Budget schedule p9 is all funds combined; lines mixing governmental and utility amounts were split using the p2 and p5/p7 breakdowns (budget_final placed only on first split item); several budget columns show 0. Business-type charges 492,925 (p2, cash received) vs 485,357 operating revenues on p7. Lottery spending put in 'other' with review. Read pages 1-10 of 10 (v8 re-trim: gained p10, Note to Budgetary Comparison Schedules, text only, nothing new). Detail (user 2026-10-27): per-fund lines from the fund statements' columns (p5, p7) replace the combined schedule.",
